Hi,

I am implementing a LaTeX 2.09 style that replaces every "picture" environment
with an empty box, and that deactivates every graphic command inside the
environment to speed-up the "draft" compilations of a document.

In this way all the floats go to the corect places and the passes needed to
get correct references are fast.

I suggest that all the graphic packages and classes in LaTeX 2e (and in future
LaTeX 3) accept the option "nopic" (or a similar standard option) so that,
with this option, all the drawing commands have an empty body.

I think that the implementors of the graphic packages are the best suited
people to make a similar modification ...

Happy LaTeX-ing
        Andrea

